1. Software Architecture

1.1 System Architecture
The Student Housing App follows a three-tier client-server architecture consisting of a mobile frontend, a REST API backend, and a relational database.

System Flow: STUDENT: Searching and Booking an Apartment

Student searches for an apartment with filters (Frontend)
Request goes to Backend
Backend checks Database (Listings Table — searches for apartments that match the price, location, and availability filters the student selected)
Backend sends matching apartment results back to Frontend
Student selects an apartment and confirms booking → stored in Database (Bookings Table — saves the student ID, listing ID, date of request, and status = Pending)


System Flow:STUDENT: Roommate Matching

Student sets preferences and budget (Frontend)
Request sent to Roommate Matching Component (Backend)
Backend queries Users Table for compatible profiles
Compatibility scores are computed and sorted
Suggested roommates returned to the student
Student initiates chat via Chat Component

STUDENT — Using the Chat

Student opens chat and sends a message to a landlord or roommate (Frontend)
Request goes to Backend
Backend checks Database (Messages Table — retrieves the conversation history between the two users)
Backend sends message history back to Frontend
Student sends new message → stored in Database (Messages Table — saves sender ID, receiver ID, message content, and timestamp)


System Flow: LANDLORD: Creating and Managing a Listing

Landlord fills in apartment details and submits a new listing (Frontend)
Request goes to Backend
Backend checks Database (Listings Table — verifies no duplicate listing exists for the same address and landlord)
Backend sends confirmation back to Frontend
Landlord confirms listing submission → stored in Database (Listings Table — saves title, description, price, location, availability date, photos, landlord ID, and status = Pending Review)


System Flow — ADMINISTRATOR: Verifying and Managing the Platform

Administrator opens the pending listings dashboard (Frontend)
Request goes to Backend
Backend checks Database (Listings Table — fetches all listings where status = Pending Review, and Reports Table — fetches all unresolved user reports)
Backend sends pending listings and reports back to Frontend
Administrator approves or rejects a listing → stored in Database (Listings Table — status updated to Verified or Rejected, and Landlord is notified)

